[00:14.31] (Alan Rose, Don Helms)
[00:16.55] One day the train was passing,
[00:17.76] I caught it comin' by
[00:20.12] To look this old world over,
[00:22.62] Under God's blue sky
[00:23.43] My darlin' stood there weepin'
[00:25.21] As I was lookin' back
[00:26.97] I kissed my baby cryin' in
[00:29.72] The smoke along the track
[00:31.33] Chorus:
[00:32.43] Bye, bye, so long,
[00:34.98] There's something down the track
[00:38.35] It's callin' me
[00:39.29] Bye, bye, so long,
[00:43.94] I guess that's just the way
[00:46.29] I'll always be
[00:47.47] Now when I get this feelin'
[00:50.88] Don't try to hold me back
[00:53.48] I'll only leave you cryin' in
